[{"id":"COR-1","class":"contract","severity":"advisory","file":"src/domain/customers.js","line":18,"what_breaks":"The email check is stricter than R-02. It refuses a domain part that starts or ends with a dot (for example 'a@b.' or 'a@.b'), but R-02 only asks for one @, text on both sides and a dot after the @. PLAN S2 Risks says 'nothing stricter'. tests/customers.test.js line 46 asserts that 'a@.' is refused, so the test locks in the stricter rule.","requirement":"R-02","evidence":"validateCustomer({name:'Ana', email:'a@b.'}): split gives local 'a' and domain 'b.'. domain.includes('.') is true, but domain.endsWith('.') is true, so isValidEmail returns false and errors.email is set. R-02 would accept this input.","proven":true},{"id":"COR-2","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/domain/orders.js","line":54,"what_breaks":"Order text filter: the list shows order numbers as '#12' (orders-view.js line 81), but typing '#12' finds nothing, because the needle is compared with String(o.number) and '12' does not contain '#'. Matching is also a substring match, so '1' matches orders 1, 10, 11 and 21. R-10 says the text matches the order number.","requirement":"R-10","evidence":"filterOrders(state, {text:'#12'}) where an order has number 12: needle is '#12', '12'.includes('#12') is false, and the customer name has no '#', so the result is [] and the UI shows 'No orders match your filter.'","proven":true},{"id":"COR-3","class":"correctness","severity":"advisory","file":"src/ui/app.js","line":19,"what_breaks":"When stored data cannot be read (R-18), ctx.state falls back to an empty state, and the lists show 'No customers yet. Use \"Add customer\" to create the first one.' and 'No orders yet...' next to the error banner. The data exists but is unreadable, so the screen states a guessed value as certain and points to an action that is disabled.","requirement":"R-18","evidence":"app.js line 13 sets locked = true when load fails. Line 19 returns emptyState because